      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Cliff from I now live in Arlington, VA (Outside Washington DC), USA",
      "description": "RCA Studio B\nBuilt by Dan Maddox in 1957, RCA Studio B first became known as one of the cradles of the \"Nashville Sound\" in the 1960s. A sophisticated style characterized by background vocals and strings, the Nashville Sound both revived the popularity of country music and helped establish Nashville as an international recording center. Hitmakers in Studio B have included Arnold, Jennings, Bobby Bare, Parton, Reeves, Willie Nelson, and Floyd Cramer, among others. For many years, Country Music Hall of Fame inductee Chet Atkins managed RCA's Nashville operation and produced hundreds of hits in Studio B.",
      "dateCreated": "2007-05-17 13:46",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "rca-studio-b-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "dn6m",
